    <item>
      <title>Chris Perruna The point of investing is to end the year (or series of investment</title>
      <link>https://t.me/realpdot/9172</link>
      <description>&lt;div class="tgme_widget_message_text js-message_text" dir="auto"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chris Perruna&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The point of investing is to end the year (or series of investments) with a net gain rather than trying to win every single trade.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Long-term profitability comes from managing risk, letting winners run and letting go of the ego-driven need to be "right" on individual positions.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Investors need to consider whether they could accept making profits by the end of the year even if the majority of their investments were losses. Most people reject this because the emotional need to be "right" overrides profitability.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Stop following the folks who want to be "right" on X and focus on the folks who are actually profitable, regardless of how many trades didn't work out.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Profitability is ALL that matters in the market.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Hint: very few are actually profitable on X&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href="https://x.com/cperruna/status/2120620924227797469" onclick="return confirm('Open this link?\n\n'+this.href);" rel="noopener" target="_blank"&gt;tweet&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
